    <mxCell id="e11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#036A6B;strokeWidth=1.6;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="clMetrics" target="alerts"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

    <mxCell id="note" value="WHY THIS CLOSES THE 23 JULY 2026 BLIND SPOT&#10;• A server-function throw is serialized to the client by the TanStack Start transport and never reaches the request middleware in start.ts or the fetch catch in server.ts, so a Postgres 42P08 broke all leave filing for four days with zero log entries.&#10;• Layer 2 sits INSIDE the server-function boundary, which is the only place the throw is observable. It logs stack + SQLSTATE, then rethrows the original error unchanged so control flow is untouched.&#10;• Every logging call is individually try-caught and fails open: a fault in the logger degrades a log line, never a request. Layer 3 is allowlist-based, so a new PII field is excluded by default rather than leaked by default.&#10;• Detection target: under 15 minutes from first occurrence, versus 4 days by employee email report." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#F5FAFA;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Montserrat;fontSize=9;fontColor=#393939;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="70" y="582" width="940" height="94" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
  </root>
